    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. And I want to be clear. I mean, I'm committed to trying to reform the party of Lincoln and Reagan. This is a party that It has a great heritage and a great history, but it needs to reimburse a bunch of its history and explain what it's about for the future, because right now, these parties really do seem addicted to a 24-hour news cycle, and, you know, pundits not picking up on your facetious rank punditry. But cable broadcast news, they need screaming chirones every three hours to try to sell more soap. I get the business model. What's weird is politicians who are willing to also think that that's their whole job. and I was joking when I said every morning but I live in Nebraska and so I fly here every Sunday night to Monday morning and when I'm getting ready to leave two of my three kids and my wife for the week every week you sort of want to say I'm making enough difference in the world and I'm headed to an institution that is really pretty content a lot of the time to just do anti and anti-anti so neither Republicans nor Democrats could tell the American people right now what their 10-year plan is for America and I don't mean 10-year plan in an East German",
