    "turn_idx": 149,
    "turn_text": "Thank you. The package will be discussed in five different segments. I think that the public doesn't trust this place, and lots of it is warranted. Some of it is sort of assumptions about this place, but we should tackle all those things, right? We shouldn't have people who have massive foreign policy responsibilities for the United States government. These are public trust roles to be director of CIA or to be the secretary of defense or to be the secretary of state, you probably ought not have your immediate family making money off speeches and raising money for foundations that are used as proto political campaigns when you have a responsibility public trust. We probably ought to have tax returns of presidents and vice presidents be disclosed as a matter of law and not just as a matter of convention that nobody ever thought to violate till the cycle and leads to massive public trust. We ought not have people come into DC planning to stay forever as lobbyists. You have a right of not just speech and assembly and religion and press but you have the right of redress and grievances. You still have a free speech right. There's no reason you need to use a network that you develop while in Congress to make money as a paid",
