    "turn_text": "that. I don't think he cares the building is actually that. I just think he wants to be enshrined eternally as an S.O.B. But I think what we should really do is talk about passing some legislation that wouldn't be able to get attention on it if it weren't for a post-maccain memorial moment. So I think there's an opportunity to have a conversation there, but I'm not naive about the fact this can take a while. But these are the kinds of longer term things we ought to be doing because the corruption in Washington, and there's lots of it, isn't a democratic problem. It isn't a Republican problem. It really is a swampy place. And every two years when there's a campaign, the party out of power runs on swamp training. And as soon as they become the party in power, they lose all interest in it. Nobody ever does any actual swamp training around here. And there's a pretty deep swamp.",
