    "turn_text": "no such thing. And I've been in office for three and a half years. And it's not every town hall, but a lot of the time when I have these public events, people think current members of Congress ran because you get your salary forever. As a pension, there's no such thing. We just get a 401k contribution just like you'd get in the private sector, and it's a fine package, but it's definitely not. I've had much better retirement package in my last few jobs than this one, but it's fine. But I think when those myths are out there having any conversation about pay, it's not the problem we should be having. We should change the incentives of the type of people who run and have it be people who view it as public service. Again, just thinking about But you can have a bed of pens, right? And you get to keep it like a lot of cool pens. Oh, I steal five or six thousand pens a month. Yeah.",
