    "turn_text": "I don't know, the polling is all over the place, right? So we're a 51-49 body right now, and if you look at the map, we should be picking up somewhere between 5 and 10 seats, and you look at the polls, and we're going to pick up somewhere between, you know, plus 5 and minus 3. It's an amazing moment, right? We've had reliable polling since the 1930s, 4 out of 5, 2-year congressional cycles the polling is useful, and 20% of the time it's just completely worthless, because there's a wave of turnout. that",
