    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90574.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 191,
    "turn_text": "imagine a bunch of people sitting around in a bar and a pub in south e and they go hey robbie you know what you're going to do you're better now you're going to texas and you're going to run as a Hispanic guy I just try to make sense of name change, but he's got a virtuous cycle of cool factor going on. The cool kids want to be with them, and then the cooler kids want to be with those cool kids. But it is strange in Texas because you have a bunch of house members who have a district that's 650 to 725,000 people. And they've got a bunch of suburban women who are very, very opposed to the president. And the fear is, again, for political consultants, if you motivate those women to turn out, the House members lose. And yet, if you don't do something to motivate a bunch of people to pay more attention to the Senate race, then that race looks harder. So I think there's a very big difference inside Texas circles about people who want the president to come do lots of rallies,",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
