    "turn_idx": 201,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, I'll let you go after this. But just one quick point I want your response here. As a political fight as a matter of sort of cultural political messaging. These victories, most of the stuff that Trump has done, that I really like, these are victories for sort of my crowd of Trump skeptics, Trump critics. The reason he adopted that list was not because of his lifelong passion about fidelity to the Constitution. The reason he adopted that list is because the Republican Party and conservative activists and donors said, look, there are some red lines you cannot cross, so your sister is out, and instead you've got to jump through some hoops to prove that you're going to do right by us on judges. And so when I hear Sean Hannity, my colleague at Fox News, talking about how this just proves Donald Trump's abiding love for the Constitution, that is what political scientists call horse crap. And the proof is that same thing with, you know, Donald Trump's commitment to pro-life politics is of recent vintage, right? And so one of the things that drives me crazy is that if you want, it's like this anonymous New York Times piece, right? First of all, I thought that was an insane thing to do. The first rule of fight club is don't talk about fight club. The first rule of secret kabals manipulating the president is don't talk about it. How come Trump's skeptical politicians and people can't take more credit for this stuff? Yeah, I mean,",
